{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,31]],"date-time":"2026-01-31T09:50:10Z","timestamp":1769853010261,"version":"3.49.0"},"reference-count":11,"publisher":"Peoples' Friendship University of Russia","issue":"2","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Metaphysics"],"abstract":"<jats:p>The article puts forward and substantiates the following thesis. A mathematical model is not sufficient to define a scientific model. A scientific model must include a conceptual model and a mathematical model built on the basis of the first. As a conceptual model, it is proposed to use ontology\u2019s, which in Computer Science are used as a representation of knowledge. It is shown that it is possible to construct ontology\u2019s for models of modern physics, in particular for models of quantum mechanics.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.22363\/2224-7580-2024-2-67-81","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,24]],"date-time":"2025-10-24T15:42:24Z","timestamp":1761320544000},"page":"67-81","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["SEMANTIC NETWORKS AND INSUFFICIENCY OF MATHEMATICAL DESCRIPTION OF SCIENTIFIC MODELS"],"prefix":"10.22363","author":[{"given":"V. I.","family":"Gurianov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"St. Petersburg State Economic University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"9635","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,15]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref1","unstructured":"\u041c\u0438\u043d\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439 \u041c. \u0424\u0440\u0435\u0439\u043c\u044b \u0434\u043b\u044f \u043f\u0440\u0435\u0434\u0441\u0442\u0430\u0432\u043b\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f \u0437\u043d\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0439 \/ \u043f\u0435\u0440. \u0441 \u0430\u043d\u0433\u043b. \u041e. \u041d. \u0413\u0440\u0438\u043d\u0431\u0430\u0443\u043c\u0430; \u043f\u043e\u0434 \u0440\u0435\u0434. \u0424. \u041c. \u041a\u0443\u043b\u043